# Files every pull request appends to. With `merge=union`, git keeps the lines both sides
# added instead of declaring a conflict, so parallel PRs do not bounce on them (herdr-agent-pool
# README, "Fewer conflicts"). Only for files where each change only adds whole lines: a union
# merge never removes lines, so check the result (scripts/check.sh) as usual. Add the project's
# own append-only files, e.g. a table of functions or a list of migrations.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
docs/decisions/README.md merge=union
docs/plan-reviews/README.md merge=union
